--cpp11
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.over.link]/6 + [dcl.fct]/3: an in-class friend declaration
of a function template with an UNNAMED parameter pack (`make(Args
&&...)`, libstdc++'s shared_ptr befriending make_shared) declares the
same template as the namespace-scope definition naming the pack.  The
parser records the `...` of the unnamed form on the declarator and of
the named form on the declarator's type; signature equivalence now
unifies the two, so the call resolves to the definition's body.
Previously the pair tied and the winner depended on candidate order --
when the bodiless friend won, std::regex's _Compiler constructor was a
havoc stub.
